**boiling point** , temperature at which the [pressure](https://www.britannica.com/science/pressure) [exerted](https://www.britannica.com/dictionary/exerted) by the surroundings upon a [liquid](https://www.britannica.com/science/liquid-state-of-matter) is equaled by the pressure exerted by the [vapour](https://www.britannica.com/science/vapor-pressure) of the liquid; under this condition, addition of [heat](https://www.britannica.com/science/heat) results in the transformation of the liquid into its vapour without raising the temperature.
