Southeast Asian cultural meaning, the survival of the cloth, the motifs, and the techniques of
their production are celebrated as evidence in support of the predominant narrative of
Southeast Asian autonomy amidst outside influence. Interestingly, the rapid industrialization
of textile production in Southeast Asia dates to the 20 th century and is connected to decline
